 ## Overview
-Global 3DGS with Progressively Growing is a sequential reconstruction method that learns a global 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) model by incrementally integrating frames, using estimated relative poses to update the scene representation and densify Gaussians to cover new views [S1]. It differs from standard global 3DGS by avoiding the accumulation of noisy relative pose errors across long sequences; instead, it grows the model frame-by-frame, aligning densification intervals with the addition of new frames to ensure continuous coverage of unobserved regions [S1].
+Global 3DGS with Progressively Growing is a sequential reconstruction method that learns a global 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) model by incrementally integrating frames, using estimated relative poses to update the scene representation and densify Gaussians to cover new views [S1]. It differs from standard global 3DGS by avoiding the dramatic impact of noisy relative poses on whole-scene optimization; instead, it grows the model frame-by-frame, aligning densification intervals with the addition of new frames to ensure continuous coverage of unobserved regions [S1].
 
